id: gap
package: bluetooth_le_siwx91x
description: >
  GAP (Generic Access Profile) component for BLE
label: GAP
category: Device|Si91x|Wireless|BLE|GAP
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
component_root_path: ./components/device/silabs/si91x/wireless/gap
provides:
  - name: gap
source:
  - path: src/gap_user_event_hdlrs.c
  - path: src/gap_init.c
  - path: src/gap_utilities.c

include:
  - path: inc
    file_list:
      - path: gap.h

config_file:
  - path: inc/gap_config.h
    directory: ble_config
    file_id: gap_config

requires:
  - name: si91x_ble_adv_scan_implementation
  - name: ble_unified_framework

template_contribution:
  - name: ble_unified_config_includes
    value: "gap_config.h"
  - name: ble_unified_init_hooks
    value:
      ble_unified_init_func: ble_gap_init
      ble_unified_init_label: "GAP"
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_MAX_NBR_PERIPHERALS(RSI_BLE_MAX_NBR_PERIPHERALS)
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_MAX_NBR_CENTRALS(RSI_BLE_MAX_NBR_CENTRALS)
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_ext_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_NUM_CONN_EVENTS(RSI_BLE_NUM_CONN_EVENTS)
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_ext_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_SET_SCAN_RESP_DATA_FROM_HOST
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_guard: RSI_BLE_SET_SCAN_RESP_DATA_FROM_HOST
  - name: ble_unified_bt_bitmap_entries
    value:
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_type: ble_ext_feature_bit_map
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_value: SL_SI91X_BLE_DISABLE_CODED_PHY_FROM_HOST
      ble_unified_bt_bitmap_guard: RSI_BLE_DISABLE_CODED_PHY_FROM_HOST
  - name: wrapper_implementations
    value:
      name: sl_btc_ble_gap_register_callbacks_wrapper
      registration_api: rsi_ble_gap_register_callbacks
      callbacks:
        - event_adv_report
        - event_conn_status
        - event_disconnect
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - NULL
        - event_enhance_conn_status
        - NULL
        - event_conn_update
        - event_remote_conn_param_req
  - name: wrapper_implementations
    value:
      name: sl_btc_ble_gap_extended_register_callbacks_wrapper
      registration_api: rsi_ble_gap_extended_register_callbacks
      callbacks:
        - event_remote_features
        - event_more_data_req
  - name: ble_events
    value:
      event_adv_report:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_adv_report
            type: rsi_ble_event_adv_report_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_adv_report
      
      event_disconnect:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_disconnect
            type: rsi_ble_event_disconnect_p
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_disconnect
      
      event_conn_status:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_conn_status
            type: rsi_ble_event_conn_status_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_conn_status
      
      event_enhance_conn_status:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_enhance_conn_status
            type: rsi_ble_event_enhance_conn_status_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_enhance_conn_status
      
      event_data_length_update:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_data_length_update
            type: rsi_ble_event_data_length_update_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_data_length_update
      
      event_phy_update:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_phy_update
            type: rsi_ble_event_phy_update_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_phy_update
      
      event_remote_conn_param_req:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_remote_conn_param_req
            type: rsi_ble_event_remote_conn_param_req_p
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_remote_conn_param_req
      
      event_conn_update:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_conn_update
            type: rsi_ble_event_conn_update_p
          - name: status
            type: uint16_t
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_conn_update
      
      event_remote_features:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_remote_features
            type: rsi_ble_event_remote_features_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_remote_features
      
      event_more_data_req:
        callback_params:
          - name: rsi_ble_event_le_dev_buf_ind
            type: rsi_ble_event_le_dev_buf_ind_p
        event_data:
          name: rsi_ble_event_le_dev_buf_ind
      
      event_advertisement_restart:
        callback_params: []
      
      event_scan_restart:
        callback_params: []
      
      conn_update_req:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t*
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
      
      connection_procedure_timeout:
        callback_params:
          - name: conn_id
            type: uint8_t
        event_data:
          name: conn_id
  - name: agents_slab
    value:
      id: gap
      context: |
        ## GAP Component (Si91x Wireless BLE Unified)
        Generic Access Profile component — owns connection state, advertising/scanning state, and the multi-protocol connection-info structure (`rsi_ble_conn_info_t`, `rsi_ble_conn_config_t`, `rsi_parsed_conf_t`). GAP is the foundation: every BLE Unified protocol component (`smp`, `gatt_*`, `legacy_adv`, `ext_adv`) `requires: gap` and reuses its types and connection table.
        ### Init hook
        - Function: `ble_gap_init` (declared as `ble_unified_init_func` — called automatically by the BLE Unified framework).
        - Registers GAP and GAP-extended callback wrappers via autogen: `sl_btc_ble_gap_register_callbacks_wrapper()` (`event_adv_report`, `event_conn_status`, `event_disconnect`, `event_enhance_conn_status`, `event_conn_update`, `event_remote_conn_param_req`) and `sl_btc_ble_gap_extended_register_callbacks_wrapper()` (`event_remote_features`, `event_more_data_req`).
        ### Configuration (`gap_config.h` — copied to `config/ble_config/`)
        Key macros the user is expected to tune per project: `RSI_BT_LOCAL_NAME`, `RSI_BLE_MAX_NBR_PERIPHERALS`, `RSI_BLE_MAX_NBR_CENTRALS`, `RSI_BLE_NUM_CONN_EVENTS`, `RSI_BLE_SET_SCAN_RESP_DATA_FROM_HOST`, `RSI_BLE_DISABLE_CODED_PHY_FROM_HOST`, `ADV_ENABLED_DEFAULT`, `SCAN_ENABLED_DEFAULT`, plus default connection parameters (interval, latency, timeout). Feature-bitmap entries (`SL_SI91X_BLE_MAX_NBR_PERIPHERALS`, `SL_SI91X_BLE_MAX_NBR_CENTRALS`, `SL_SI91X_BLE_NUM_CONN_EVENTS`) are contributed automatically.
        ### Public header rule
        `gap.h` lives next to the default `gap_config.h` in the component's `inc/` folder. It includes `<gap_config.h>` (angle brackets) so the user-editable copy under `config/ble_config/` always wins over the SDK default. Quoted includes from `gap.h` would silently pick the SDK default due to GCC's same-directory rule.
        ### Common Mistakes to Avoid
        - Calling `rsi_ble_gap_register_callbacks()` directly from app code — the wrapper is owned by autogen.
        - Configuring more peripherals/centrals in `gap_config.h` than the firmware's connection table supports — values are validated by the controller and excess configurations cause init to fail.
        - Updating connection parameters from inside a connection-event callback before the previous procedure has completed — use the `event_conn_update` callback to gate further updates.
    priority: -5303
